{"ts":"2026-09-05T19:06:23.505Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-astra","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bc5f6d24074543521094561e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-astra","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Report and scope\n\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1203\n\nImprove the reported warning-close then already-terminal refusal sequence with an executable recovery command. Existing warn/require policy and atomic structured close evidence are shipped contracts; preserve them. A normal pm update can append missing expected_result and actual_result while keeping the item terminal. Do not imply that force, reopen, or rewriting the original close event is required.\n\n## Reported reproduction\n\n## Summary\n\n`pm close` accepts a close that it simultaneously reports as incomplete, and the obvious next command — re-running `close` with the flags the warning names — is rejected. The warning therefore steers an agent into a blocked retry.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```\n$ pm close pm-linear-tfj7 --author pi-orchestrator --resolution \"...\"\nclose_reason: \"...\"\nwarnings:\n  - \"close_validation_missing_fields:pm-linear-tfj7:expected_result (--expected-result),actual_result (--actual-result)\"\n```\n\nThe item is now closed, and the warning names two flags of `pm close`. Supplying them:\n\n```\n$ pm close pm-linear-tfj7 --author pi-orchestrator \\\n    --resolution \"...\" --expected-result \"...\" --actual-result \"...\"\nError: Command failed\nWhat happened:\n  Item pm-linear-tfj7 is already terminal; use --force to close again.\n```\n\nThe only advertised way forward is `--force`, which reads as an override for re-closing a settled item — not as the way to finish a record the CLI just told you was unfinished.\n\n`pm update` does work and is the correct path, but nothing in either message points to it:\n\n```\n$ pm update pm-linear-tfj7 --author pi-orchestrator --expected-result \"...\" --actual-result \"...\"\nstatus: \"closed\"\nchanged_field_count: 2\n```\n\n## Why this matters for agents\n\nThe warning is well-formed and machine-readable, so an agent will act on it, and the action it implies is the one operation that is refused. The three plausible agent responses are all wrong: retry `close` (rejected), add `--force` (a destructive-sounding escape hatch used for a non-destructive completion), or ignore the warning (leaves the acceptance evidence the governance policy asked for permanently missing).\n\n## Expected\n\nEither:\n\n1. `close` completes the record when it is re-run on a terminal item with only the missing fields — no `--force`, since nothing is being overwritten; or\n2. the warning names the command that actually works, e.g. `pm update <id> --expected-result … --actual-result …`; or\n3. the close is refused up front when `governance.require_close_reason`-style validation is unmet, rather than succeeding and reporting the gap afterwards.\n\nOption 3 is the most consistent with how `require_close_reason` itself behaves — that one *does* fail closed:\n\n```\nError: Close reason text is required because governance.require_close_reason is enabled\n```\n\nTwo adjacent close-validation rules currently fail in opposite directions: one blocks the close, the other lets it through with a warning that cannot then be acted on.\n\n## Environment\n\n@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.5, Linux, Node 22.\n\n## Delivery boundary\n\nIntake only in PR #1204. This item remains open and unclaimed; no implementation or reproduction success is asserted. Implement through the public SDK with thin CLI adapters and executable negative controls before closing."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-ub1ott"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1203: Offer actionable acceptance-evidence backfill after a warning close"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Improve the reported warning-close then already-terminal refusal sequence with an executable recovery command. Existing warn/require policy and atomic structured close evidence are shipped contracts; preserve them. A normal pm update can append missing expected_result and actual_result while keeping the item terminal. Do not imply that force, reopen, or rewriting the original close event is required."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-05T19:06:23.505Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-05T19:06:23.505Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A temporary CLI workflow closes with missing structured fields and receives a directly runnable update recovery command; Applying the recovery preserves terminal status and the immutable original close event while appending new evidence; Require-mode refusal and complete-field silent close behavior remain compatible; SDK and CLI structured recovery fields identify the actual permitted mutation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Reduce recovery ambiguity and preserve trustworthy project context for agents"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"A reproducible SDK contract with actionable CLI recovery and regression evidence"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"New user report GH-1203 during PR #1204 final integration"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.9.5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"sdk/lifecycle"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1203","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:23.505Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"global","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-f05lsg","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:23.505Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-mpbb","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:23.505Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-wenq","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:23.505Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:23.505Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"\"text=Duplicate-check evidence: strict complete all-status corpus contained 2642 items, including terminal history; exact GitHub issue URL was absent. Request-specific search and current open/in_progress inventories were read. Full live predecessor pm-wenq and parent pm-mpbb metadata plus verified history were inspected. This report extends a distinct boundary beyond the closed predecessor and is not a duplicate. Intake remains open and unclaimed.\""}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-05T19:06:23.505Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"\"text=Improve the reported warning-close then already-terminal refusal sequence with an executable recovery command. Existing warn/require policy and atomic structured close evidence are shipped contracts; preserve them. A normal pm update can append missing expected_result and actual_result while keeping the item terminal. Do not imply that force, reopen, or rewriting the original close event is required.\""}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":"src/sdk/lifecycle/close.ts","scope":"project","note":"Existing implementation boundary to reproduce and improve"},{"path":"tests/unit/commands/close-command.spec.ts","scope":"project","note":"Existing regression suite to extend; no new regression is claimed"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/docs","value":[{"path":"docs/COMMANDS.md","scope":"project","note":"Existing public contract to preserve and clarify"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"afc891765a99b5e51270e0538784bb2ddafcced1e9c3f99c94f6ac97871f36b5","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d58b32c6ddcc4d73ef43aee577965c051c85eea392aee77e52a1c8af0c800627"}
